                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df6c0541-809f-34e1-a7a2-c445ca8c9566",
                        "entry_id": "f03d1660-d275-3f2f-8f8a-e481fec0014e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to the culture of Washington, D.C.; politicized."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "01b863c6-7ce9-420d-a7b1-5170745759b5",
                                "sense_id": "df6c0541-809f-34e1-a7a2-c445ca8c9566",
                                "text": "Apparently wishing to go Beltway in a big way, the Gap reportedly solicited Clinton spokesman George Stephanopoulos and media adviser Mandy Grunwald to pose for ads, but were turned down."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39111bc3-8ac4-4ff5-b430-bd3dc79acdab",
                                "sense_id": "df6c0541-809f-34e1-a7a2-c445ca8c9566",
                                "text": "In a typical indictment, one columnist recently called some piece of Washington policymaking \"too secret, too expert, too Beltway.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2c6cde1-c788-4643-b327-6eb0cec50d91",
                                "sense_id": "df6c0541-809f-34e1-a7a2-c445ca8c9566",
                                "text": "2002 http://www.pbs.org/wgbh/pages/frontline/shows/schools/nochild/lemann.html\nYour New Yorker article posed the question, \"Can the president's education crusade survive Beltway politics?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3184295b-033e-4239-9086-41e1041b2c22",
                                "sense_id": "df6c0541-809f-34e1-a7a2-c445ca8c9566",
                                "text": "And wouldn't you know, the real-life Dean, in a real-life debate, used a line the show's writers had proposed for him. Nothing more Beltway than that."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "78fe621a-1e07-4de5-9229-4c77cfa5e26b",
                                "sense_id": "df6c0541-809f-34e1-a7a2-c445ca8c9566",
                                "text": "Then he went Beltway and started rooting for the Orioles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
